Consider the following classes:

    class Mouse{
        public void behaviour() {
            System.out.println("Squeek, Squeek!");
        }
    }

    class FatMouse extends Mouse {
        public void behaviour(int n){
            for (int i = 0; i < n; i++)
                System.out.println("Eat Cheese!");
        }
    }

    class FatterMouse extends FatMouse {
        public void behaviour(){
            System.out.println("Sleep, Sleep!");
        }
    }

What output will the following code snippet produce?

    FatMouse charlie  = new FatterMouse();
    Mouse mouse = charlie;

    charlie.behaviour();
    charlie.behaviour(3);
